## Implementation findings (beyond the frozen notes)

1. TWO extra root causes found by measurement, both in-family:
   a. `--path-conn-up` angle had the mirrored x-sign (atan2(sway - prev, dy))
      so every UP stub pointed AWAY from its previous ring — the owner's
      "stray stub" / "N3->N4 stray" in the before image. Fixed sign; the
      R3 "keep the math" rule is honoured (down/up now share one formula).
   b. Stub anchors `top: calc(100% - .3rem)` left the drawn line OFFSET from
      the center-to-center segment (parallel by ~7px at sway extremes). The
      stubs now anchor ON the ring center (top/bottom: 50%) so the rotated
      line IS the segment; A2's midpoint check hits it exactly.
2. The row-height fix needed MORE than `height: 76px`: the inner grid track
   auto-grows to the tallest item (a 110px unlock-hint row pushed the ring
   19px off-lattice even with a fixed box — and bare `1fr` is minmax(AUTO,1fr)).
   The invariant is `height: 4.75rem` + `grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr)` +
   column `gap: 0`; long label stacks spill symmetrically in the text column.
   Evidence: capture-interim-reds.log (pair 9/10 at 94.7/57.3 pre-minmax).
3. Pinned-row yield: title clamps to one line at the row top, "You are here"
   absolute at the row bottom (right of ring), progress line suppressed on the
   pill row (the ring fill arc encodes it). First green screenshot showed the
   capsule still kissing the title; margin-top -0.35rem lift fixed it,
   re-verified visually (8-10px gap in the crop review).

